WEBVTT

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:03.440
In a universe somewhere

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.470
...is a galaxy somewhere...

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.380
Within which somewhere is a planet:

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.120
Earthdash.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.170
There, when you look up at the sky,

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.330
you see a city called Mooneyes on the face of the moon.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:19.180
Brighter than the sun during the day,

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.300
and shining more beautifully than the stars at night,

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:27.590
it is a symbol of hopes and dreams to the people.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.050
They all dream of someday living on the moon...

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.310
DESTROY

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.310
DESTROY

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:04.010
Is something wrong, Princess?

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:08.040
I feel some sort of vital spirit stirring there.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.370
That is Rollingtown, the next destination on your tour, is it not? {sz: sounds like she's doing political visits or something}

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.980
It seems they're amidst a building boom, so it must be under construction at the moment.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.190
Hey!

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:30.950
Hey!

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:32.080
{chi sound} What?!

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:33.630
Where's he aiming from?

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:34.380
How should I know?

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.420
This happened because you're a stupid-head!

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:39.260
What are they? Shells?

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:40.090
No, it's different!

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:44.460
A ball?

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.350
Wait... Dunk Mask?

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:55.610
What are you gonna do?

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.180
What are you doing, stupid-head?!

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:01.020
If that hit you in the head, you'd get even stupider!

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:01.860
Shut up!

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:04.340
I'll be damned if I'm gonna let an opponent turn
 his back on me when I can't even see his face!

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:06.780
So will you promise to run away once you see his face?!

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.780
I'll decide that after I get a look!

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.780
You'll die! We're gonna die!

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:16.670
Shit!

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.240
Huh? He's gone!

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.170
Shut up! What's done is done!

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.920
Just figure out where he is A.S.A.P!

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.180
You're being too loud for me to hear!

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:33.190
There!

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.800
Hell yeah, let's go!

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.040
You go get killed and good riddance!

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:53.370
I've got you now!

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.230
Hey, where is he?

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:58.560
I don't know!

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.420
I just heard a sound, that's all.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:01.530
I'm gonna eat you, you little—

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:02.640
What a coincidence!

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.880
I was just thinking of how I was in the mood to eat a stupid-head!

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:07.430
To your right!

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:07.960
What is?

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:08.850
A ball, a ball!

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:10.290
What? From where?

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.200
Damn!

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:20.120
He really is a rock head.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.900
Nice of him to be the bait and all...

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:25.990
From this position I can see everything with ease.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:28.160
He's there!

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:33.040
You're mine!

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:49.950
Th-That's...

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.280
Does he plan to use as many balls as he needs...

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:54.390
...to take us both on?!

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:08.210
God dammit!

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:10.230
I h-hate this!

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.650
I hate that he beat me, but

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:13.500
welling up from deep within me... {I know japs love to refer to themselves as their bodies and shit but whateverz. It's engrish.}

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.160
...is such bliss...

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.590
I like it!

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:24.000
Whoa, no kidding around!

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.520
They're both trashed to bits.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.340
Now this is worth fixing!

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:31.050
All right! You two go and eat dinner or something for now. Go, go!

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:34.180
We have all that food, so go eat! Eat!

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:36.870
There's no way I'm gonna let that bastard slide!

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:40.450
A bastard, you say... Well that doesn't narrow down the list of suspects...

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:43.440
Not just anyone can throw the balls like he threw them.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:45.320
I'm gonna track him down!

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:46.570
And you?

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:49.640
I don't know.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:50.760
Pathetic.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:54.560
You got so close, and still didn't get a glimpse of a face or two! {sz: lit he says "one face or two faces". Dan is maybe not so good at the sentences}

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.070
As if you got close at all.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:02.770
Sela?

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:03.540
I'm going home.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:04.500
Take care of the repairs for me.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:06.060
Thanks for the business!

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:07.820
It'll take a little while.

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:10.110
I wonder if that girl's okay.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.100
"Girl"? What girl?

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.640
Now, don't get all cranky just because you lost, Legend.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.010
I didn't lose!

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.520
Look! Word has spread already!

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:21.910
"Dunk Mask Reappears!"

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:25.940
"The end of a legend and the beginning of something new?"

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.530
"L-L-Leg-Legen..."

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:31.780
"Legend"!

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:38.750
"Dunk Mask, the Debt King, took on the Platinum Hurricane Sela D. Miranda in a 1-on-1 match and lost."

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:42.600
"Furthermore, he was cast deep into adversity when a mysterious long shooter...

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:45.860
...appeared and destroyed his beloved mech."

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:49.600
"Bigfoot City Basketball is currently in the throes of a multipartite power struggle. {sz: lol this "multipartite power struggle" word is an extremely high-level kanji phrase that is supposed to be confusing.}

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:53.790
We could well describe it as an era where opportunity awaits the truly talented, no matter who they are."

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.350
"Ultimate Bystander, signing off."

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:57.710
{heeeh sound} That girl earlier—

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:01.100
She's called the Platinum Hurricane! That's so cool.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:02.590
What a load of bull.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:04.830
"Debt King"? What's with that?! "Debt King"?!

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.560
Well, you can't blame them.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:08.220
It's true, after all.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.640
What?!

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:15.340
But really, these City Basketball columns sure get updated fast.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:16.560
I don't like it!

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:19.020
There's someone sneaking around spying on me.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.250
What are you gonna do, Dan?

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:39.640
That man... He might be...

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:43.940
Why hello there, my lonely-looking little lady!

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:47.790
A lady like you needs someone to comfort her, and I guess that someone is me.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:52.800
Are you any good? {I'm going to go out on a limb on this one. I know the jap is something like strong, amazing, etc. But, judging from how this crazy women thinks, it's seems she wants someone who's a challenge to her skills hence, why i went with "any good" which would double as a sexual innuendo joke too!}

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:58.190
Oh, enough to make a quiet little lady cry out, gasp, and burst into tears five times over!

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:05.770
Waste of my time.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:09.260
You all could bundle your genes in a nice variety pack and I'd still pass.

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:12.530
Honestly.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.550
Men are like wet paper bags, every last one of 'em. {sz: lol, this is lit "All the men I meet are totally weak." It's very similar to her "bottom-of-the-barrel men" line from ep1. The wet paper bag thing is meant to be a reference to the "kitten in a wet paper bag" expression.}

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:20.100
{kya!} Billy! Are you okay?! {these words are hard to hear but are buried in the general "kyaa!"}

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:21.420
Hold on!

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:22.680
It hurts!

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:23.780
{bg} Don't die!

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:26.370
I guess if boys will be boys, then girls will be girls.

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:36.860
I won't let anyone walk over me and get away with it.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:40.260
But... What I want is...

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:42.240
Are you all right?

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:49.210
A beautiful woman with a seductive look— that's just asking for trouble.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:52.050
Iceman?

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:54.630
I'm surprised you know of me.

00:07:56.510 --> 00:08:00.220
One year ago, when Dunk Mask was running wild in Rolling Arena,

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:01.850
you blocked him...

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:08.010
Oh, that was a painful day.

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:10.360
By that point it wasn't even a real match anymore.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.930
You should go home.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:16.540
Won't be long before the moonlight fades.

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:18.850
Moon moon.

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:25.480
This is the moonside-originated Moonbeam Broadcast System, MBS. {Broadcast since later down it says Broadcast. Consistency}

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:28.940
This ends tonight's broadcast.

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:33.370
This is the Moonbeam Broadcast System, MBS.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.070
So, shall I escort you?

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:43.480
If something is troubling you, I'd be glad to offer my counseling services on the way.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:47.270
I suppose so. I might have to ask you all sorts of questions.

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:51.860
I can't stop wondering who and where the man is...

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:54.050
...who made me feel this way!

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:03.670
Do you play streetball?

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:08.460
That isn't basketball, sadly.

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:12.780
It seems you may have mistaken me for someone else.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:16.620
I am a Bigfoot Basketball player, Iceman Hottie.

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:20.120
I only fight when I play Bigfoot Basketball.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:22.400
Hey, Iceman.

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:27.260
Would you consider giving me your genes?

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:28.410
Once would be enough.

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:31.270
You're an interesting young woman.

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:32.810
I'm Sela. Sela Miranda.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.700
Good night, Sela.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:47.470
He actually made me blush.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.460
Incredible...

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:57.510
This statue was erected to memorialize the Dunk Mask incident,

00:09:57.510 --> 00:10:01.760
which occurred last year when this was still a Bigfoot Basketball arena.

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:05.080
It was Dunk Mask who destroyed the match and also destroyed the arena.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:10.170
The sight had such a profound impact on our youth, that it lead them to them to cherish their own hopes and dreams...

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.570
...and became an awe-inspiring legend that is still passed down today!

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:15.770
Destroyed, you say?! How barbaric!

00:10:15.770 --> 00:10:18.270
Truly, the things which these vulgar savages contrive are—

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:21.520
Jiiya, endeavors such as these by the common people {'jiiya' –ê‚â appears more like an abbreviation of a title or a nickname than a real name — the "jii" is the kanji for "old man" — but it's not any family relationship term and I have no idea how to translate it if it's a nickname. So romaji it is.}

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:24.660
are what support the lifestyle which we enjoy at the royal palace.

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:26.070
Do not be rude.

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:28.030
Yes, Princess.

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:30.030
But you know?

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:35.080
Isn't it a bit weird to say it's "still passed down today" when it's only been a year?

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:36.880
If it makes us money, I don't care.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:40.460
Step on up, we got your Dunk Mask shirts and Dunk Mask towels right here!

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.300
Everyone, be careful!

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:48.760
Destroy!

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:01.070
Wh-What is this, huh?

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.970
Ganz, you think maybe this is...

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.280
...a declaration of war?

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:08.310
What is this? Anti-Establishment terrorism?!

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:10.160
Be calm, everyone.

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:14.540
The aura of anger has already vanished.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:34.430
Destroy!

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:42.440
Destroy!

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:56.590
Coco!

00:11:56.590 --> 00:11:58.930
So this is how you ended up...!

00:11:58.930 --> 00:12:00.630
Good grief, just take a better look at it!

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:02.400
It's your stupid head.

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:06.190
Probably the work of the same ones who attacked you guys yesterday, Dan.

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:06.590
What?!

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:07.610
Those too.

00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:09.520
Oh, this is amazing!

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:12.460
I've never seen such a mountain of trashed mechs before.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.720
Excellent job in getting them so totaled, guys!

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:20.000
You all had better take some time to recuperate too.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:20.710
Yes, sir.

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:23.320
Oh yeah, there's this too.

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:26.490
What the hell?!

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:29.660
Destroy, that bastard!

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:43.630
Excuse me, I have a Bigfoot that needs some repairs—

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:45.290
What, <i>another</i> one?!

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:48.490
I fix them and I fix them and yet there's still more!

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:52.120
Dan! Do something about this!

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:53.580
What do you mean, "do something"?

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.600
Get rid of that Destroy guy.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:57.600
No need to strain yourself asking me.

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:58.850
I'm gonna get even with him myself.

00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:00.350
Then hurry up about it!

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:02.100
That's what I'm figuring out now!

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:05.000
For starters, there's no way to know what direction he'll be attacking from!

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:05.570
So I...

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:07.110
In that case figure it out faster!

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:09.170
I'm trying!

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:12.530
That's right! He's a pea-brain so it takes time!

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:14.490
While you're lolling around here,

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:17.810
people who don't operate Bigfoots might start getting hurt too.

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:22.220
Coco...

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:27.120
I'm willing to join forces to get rid of him.

00:13:27.650 --> 00:13:29.940
Oh, it's the Platitude Hotpad.

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:31.910
Platinum Hurricane!

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:35.720
It might be someone you know.

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:40.480
I don't know anyone that vicious.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:43.810
We can't afford to wait until Dan thinks of something.

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:45.230
We just have to get rid of him.

00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:49.840
But it's hard to do that when you don't know when or from what direction he'll attack.

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:52.150
And even if you do get close, you'd get taken out instantly...

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:54.240
It'd be great if we could get behind him, huh?

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:00.550
Hey kid. This is your pet, right?

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:03.050
Spanky, what are you eating?

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:04.130
I'm ashamed. {sz: apparently, ashamed to be eating just a mouse and not someone's ankle or something.}

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:08.050
Out of everyone I know, you're the most vicious.

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:10.430
That's it!

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:11.140
What is?

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:13.450
We just have to lure him to us!

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:14.720
How?

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:24.930
Fire safety!

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:32.090
Dunk Mask says only you can prevent fires!

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:36.100
What's fire safety? {lol, they aren't quite as dumb as this exchange suggests. It's sort of a weird historical phrase in JP and if you just heard it you would think it was talking about a person, not a state of mind. But tling it to some weird phrase like "thermal amelioration" just made this whole thing weird, not funny.}

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:36.990
How should I know?

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:38.920
It's not a food, that's for sure!

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:44.750
Dunk Mask is fire safety!

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:49.120
The instant warning system, Dunk Mask!

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:52.690
He dunks in a mask and is careful with matches!

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:56.180
Destroy!

00:14:57.890 --> 00:14:59.850
Destroy, destroy, destroy!

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:01.110
Destroy!

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:08.290
Fire safety!

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:13.790
Dunk Mask is here!

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:14.670
What?!

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:20.700
Destroy!

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:29.790
This is...

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:35.750
Fire safety!

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:41.390
I thought it was you, Iceman Hottie.

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:44.560
{tape}I'm gonna catch you, Destroy!

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:48.200
I thought you said you didn't play streetball.

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:56.610
This isn't basketball.

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:58.200
It's Destroy!

00:15:59.010 --> 00:15:59.530
What?!

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:01.780
You hog the ball too much!

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:03.350
I see.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:05.160
He <i>is</i> someone I know.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:06.500
Perfect.

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:08.180
I owe you a year-old debt,

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:10.310
and I'm gonna pay it back ten billionfold!

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:13.050
But I think just one ball is enough.

00:16:15.770 --> 00:16:16.900
Let's go.

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:18.220
Three...

00:16:18.650 --> 00:16:19.550
Two...

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:20.800
One...

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:21.890
Zero!

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:25.430
Why you!

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:26.770
You aren't getting away!

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:28.620
My head!

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:30.860
Look, it's empty inside, what did I tell you?

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:34.980
Dammit, those two...

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:45.870
The night air is bad for your health, Princess.

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:48.790
Mixed with the wind is the same aura that I felt then...

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:50.940
No... One more wild.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:54.560
That is most likely the effect of the vulgar inhabitants overflowing this city—

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:57.920
Princess! Princess! That is dangerous!

00:16:58.220 --> 00:17:00.650
Please stop! Princess!

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:04.400
What is that?

00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:07.300
A ball? A basket?

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:16.550
He hasn't trained.

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:19.820
Someone like that wasted our match and gets treated like a legend?!

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:22.020
What bullshit! I won't allow it!

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:25.240
I'll take his streetball and destroy it!

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:26.430
Gotcha!

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:29.160
So you bear a grudge against Dan, then?

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:32.500
I merely intend to crush all streetball players.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:35.420
Of course that includes you, young lady!

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:37.850
Sounds promising.

00:17:37.850 --> 00:17:39.820
Try it then if you can.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:41.970
I'll turn the tables and grind you in my hand.

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:46.430
And when dawn breaks, I'll have your genes!

00:17:47.470 --> 00:17:49.290
What the hell are you talking about?!

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:51.660
Don't think you can ignore me!

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:55.340
Man, it's loud out here.

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:56.690
What's exploding anyway?

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:01.700
Hey, what's the deal?

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:06.330
It's no use. I really drank too much.

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:07.790
That way!

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:22.470
Good, good. Later we'll put this on the Net and make a hefty mint.

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:26.510
But I wonder, why don't those three punch or kick or anything?

00:18:26.510 --> 00:18:29.720
If it's a free-for-all beatdown, wouldn't that way be faster?

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:32.380
Sometimes you come up with some radical ideas!

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:35.100
But it's because those three are basketball players.

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:38.540
It's their style to do it that way.

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:40.890
I guess that could work out... Whoa!

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:55.900
Destiny... There's destiny in the wind.

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:03.420
Destroy, destroy, destroy!

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:04.680
Outta the way, Purapura!

00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:06.210
I told you it's Platinum!

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:11.600
Just a sec! Don't get too full of yourself!

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:13.410
You bastard!

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:37.500
<i>Destroy!</i>

00:19:41.270 --> 00:19:42.000
Crap!

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:44.090
Dan! It's the cops! Time to split!

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:45.380
Hurry!

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.970
...Des...troy...

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:05.010
It's over.

00:20:06.210 --> 00:20:08.990
Those people were amazing!

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:15.370
Princess! Hurry and come down, please!

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:27.140
Good grief. Every single time, he comes back the worse for wear.

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:29.550
Good, good.

00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:31.990
This baby is gonna get better and better.

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:36.580
Dunk Mask's Dangan Deliveries— Is this the place?

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:37.690
Yes, thanks for—

00:20:38.110 --> 00:20:38.940
Huge—!

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:41.770
So that boy is Dunk Mask?

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:50.480
Leave all the rest to me.

00:20:50.480 --> 00:20:52.920
I'm going to be your producer.

00:20:53.470 --> 00:20:57.190
Yes, me, Haruka Gracia, a woman from the moon. {No official last name spelling that I've seen}

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:58.750
Count your blessings.

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:02.230
H-Hey, Dan.

00:21:02.230 --> 00:21:04.180
Y-Yeah... There's no doubt.

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:05.380
Those are real.

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:08.170
She got us... that woman.

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:14.650
What <i>is</i> a Lunar bust anyway?!

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:17.290
Means you were beat at your own game and have nothing to stand on now.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:19.250
She wants to book matches for Dan and the others?!

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:21.570
They're not a bunch that will listen to her because of her bust!

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:26.980
Next time, Three-way Free Fight.

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:26.980
NEXT TIME

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:26.980
THREE-WAY

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:26.980
FREE FIGHT

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:26.880
Sounds cutthroat.
